    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d22e54be-b5f1-5c49-8a85-41eefebefd55",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $3?$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -6 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $C$ since it has only $2$ columns. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $A$ has exactly $3$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$ As we can see, the matrix $B$ has exactly $3$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(B)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $B$ only.\"",
